    "summary": "Blazing Dark Star, relentless Other One>Cryptical, high‑energy psychedelia",
    "blurb": "The show launches from a crisp 'Morning Dew' into an incendiary Dark Star that segues into a nonstop Other One > Cryptical marathon. Eleven propels the set while Pigpen blows the doors off on Lovelight and Billy’s drumming stays wildly tight.",
    "review": "February 6, 1969 at St. Louis’ Kiel Auditorium captures the Dead in peak psychedelic form. After an opening Dew that takes a few seconds to settle, Jerry Garcia launches into a scorching Dark Star whose tone and swagger are repeatedly praised – even his cheeky “We have some more time…” banter becomes part of the magic. The band then rolls straight into a high‑energy stretch of Saint Stephen, The Eleven and a blistering Turn On Your Lovelight before diving into a wild Other One > Cryptical sequence that includes both Cryptical Envelopments and a burst of feedback, leaving listeners “dripping with goo.” Pigpen’s organ on Lovelight is described as blowing the door off, and Billy Kreutzmann is called “nuts on the drums,” driving the relentless momentum. The soundboard capture (gd69‑02‑06.sbd.cotsman.6284.sbeok.shnf) is clear after the brief opener, presenting the full set with a mix that lets every instrument shine.",
